# Toward exclusion of the L₃(2) core quotient

The commutator-core development proves the final group-theoretic reduction
of 15.3.23: Q = [O₂(L),L] is nontrivial, lies in S, and its conjugate pair
is normalized once the source core-action bounds are constructed.

The L₃(2) exclusion still requires the C.1.34 chief-factor comparison,
both fixed-space branches, both choices of Hypothesis 15.3.10, and the
model-dependent conjugate-core bounds. The conditional reduction exported
here does not assert those conclusions or the completed source theorem.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.23, printed pp.1128–1129 (PDF pp.1145–1146).
